{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KiZNVUPYgVuMmDU5ki","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote it with the facts you gave me and left out anything you didn't know. It's about 360 words.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Request for promotion to Senior Paralegal\n\nDear David,\n\nI'd like to be considered for promotion to Senior Paralegal in the January review cycle. I've been a paralegal in the litigation group for five years. I already do much of what the senior role covers: I train our paralegals and keep the group's deadlines reliable.\n\nLast year I supported four lawyers on 23 cases, two of which went to trial. I billed 1,640 hours against the group's target of 1,550.\n\nIn 2023 I built the court-deadline tracking sheet our group uses, and two other groups in the firm have since adopted it. I'd also like you to hear about one mistake from me directly. Last March I entered a filing deadline wrong in that sheet. Another paralegal caught it, and we filed two hours before the court's cutoff. After that I added a second-person check to the sheet. Since the check went in last April, the sheet has logged about 600 entries with no wrong or missed deadlines. I can't promise I'll never make an error. What I can do is build checks that catch errors before they reach a court, and that's what I did here.\n\nI've also trained the three paralegals the group hired over the past two years. Two are still with us, and one left after eight months. Supervising the paralegals formally would make this part of my job rather than something I fit in around it.\n\nIf promoted, I will:\n\n- Hold a short weekly check-in with the paralegals I supervise, so workload and deadline problems come up early.\n- Complete the state paralegal certification by June 2027.\n\nI know the senior role carries a $9,000 increase. I don't know whether a senior position is currently open or budgeted. If it isn't, I'd value your view on what it would take.\n\nI'd appreciate the chance to talk with you in person before requests are due on December 15. Please let me know a time that works for you.\n\nThank you for considering this.\n\nBest regards,\nJenna Morales\n</final_document>\n\n- **The March error:** I put it in on purpose. The tracking sheet is your strongest point, so David is likely to hear about the mistake anyway, and it lands better coming from you along with the fix and the 600-entry record. I didn't claim that the other two groups use the check.\n- **The paralegal who left:** I stated it plainly and gave no reason, because I don't know one. If there was a reason unrelated to the training (a move, a different career), adding a few words would help.\n- **Worth adding if you can:** a sentence of support from one of your four lawyers, by name. This could be from one of the trials. It's the main thing the letter is missing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":10174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":745},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"990564b9-e9de-40df-8349-6cf76a3e7fe5","uuid":"c4b6879a-22cd-479d-ac2b-f8039ce6d457","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:33:38.518Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KiZCpcxPeHqzRj3iXE"}
